WEBVTT

00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:14,220
I have a lot of cramping in my legs and sometimes my big toe. What could be the problem

00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:20,460
besides magnesium and mineral deficiency? So you're right. The first thing you think of

00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:27,100
is leg cramping and your toe cramping is magnesium, mineral deficiency, iron deficiency are all

00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:34,780
things. However, there's another thing that can be common with muscle cramping in your legs,

00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:42,300
which hardly anybody thinks about. It can be tied to food allergies as well. I know some patients

00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:49,740
that have gluten sensitivities that kind of fall off the wagon and start eating gluten again,

00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:57,340
and they end up with cramping and or pain in their lower extremities. That's not an uncommon

00:00:57,340 --> 00:01:10,450
thing as well. I would do take-backs with epsom salts could be helpful. Those are the kind of things

00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:16,450
that you look for. At a blood test, make sure that your iron isn't really low or you're at your

00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:26,450
really adiabic as well.

